.\" Update for the -B fall-through fix in procrule.c 1.23. Removes the BUGS section entirely, since the -B entry was its only content and an empty heading is worse than none. Drops the See BUGS cross-reference and the do-not-combine--B-with--s workaround from the -B option, both now stale. -B gains the accurate current behaviour: counts of zero or less are rejected, and -B composes with -s. Keeps one paragraph of history under -B, because a reader on a pre-1.23 build still gets a zero-byte file named after the count and would otherwise have no explanation for it. TH version bumped 1.22 to 1.23. Renders warning-free under groff -man -ww.
